BuildX 2026 · Banking, Financial Services & FinTech · MuleCatch enhancement

MuleCatch risk engine: system design

The pilot (shadow-scoring 5 % of a mid-size bank's UPI payments) fits on one machine, provided the graph clustering that finds mule rings moves
off the per-payment path. Scoring every payment of the whole bank needs about 20 CPU cores of scoring workers behind a stream. Mule detection
stays at the centre. Three new engines add session, beneficiary and behaviour context around it, and a false-positive control layer decides when the
evidence is strong enough to interrupt a customer.

Proposal v1 · 4 November 2026 · builds on the repository at commit f22e7f2 (Railway branch with the latest upstream work merged) · for review, not an approved
design or deployment · synthetic data only; no customer data was read, created or sent anywhere

1 · Today's system 2 · Unified engine 3 · False-positive control

